After the merge pass folds two producers' records for one declaration, the
record must say who holds each value and what the other producer said.
Until now the pass copied the incumbent and kept the candidate set only in
memory.

The slot (§6; SCHEMA_VERSION 0.20.10 -> 0.20.11, additive). Symbol and Edge
gain `attribution` ({field: [pass_id, ...]} — the producers whose value the
scalar slot carries: both on agreement, the arbitration winner on a
contest, the sole observer otherwise) and `alternatives` ({field: [{value,
origin: [pass_id, ...]}]}, present only for contested fields — nothing a
producer emitted is discarded, §1). Dict-valued, so no `# axis:` line: the
keys are field names of the record and the leaves pass ids. to_dict emits
them only when set and from_dict reads them back, so a single-producer
artifact is byte-identical; the schema generator declares both conditional
and populates them on its round-trip samples; docs/schema.json regenerated.

The arbitration property (§4). merge_producers.arbitrate(candidates,
precedence) is a pure function over the candidate set with ONE stamped
default — precedence in incumbent_first order for every categorical
attribute (the §5 built-in until WI-hukuf reads it from config.toml); span
is the one exception, decided by the item-role member. _stamp_slot
arbitrates every tracked attribute (name, kind, stable_id, span, signature,
docstring, qualified_name, visibility, modifiers, is_exported), sets the
scalar and writes the slot in one step; the pass no longer copies the
incumbent. An alternative policy is an opt-in read of the same candidates.

Corroboration (§13; CONFIDENCE_MODEL v2.0 -> v2.1). The merge pass now folds
the participants' agreeing edges itself (§11) — incumbent-first survivor,
the others' call sites absorbed through _absorb_call_site, origin union,
edge_key reset, origin_run_id = the producer-merge run — rather than leaving
them to deduplicate_edges, whose survivor is encounter order (the SCIP arm
runs first by priority, so it would have kept the wrong one). Two DISTINCT
inference pathways (different evidence_type) on one (src, dst, edge_type)
make the survivor `corroborated` — a new confidence_source value, in the
validator's bounded enum — at the declared CORROBORATED_CONFIDENCE of 0.95,
never max (which launders an emitter constant) nor noisy-OR (the producers
read the same text), with both originals in alternatives.confidence; the
same pathway twice is not new evidence and keeps the incumbent's value and
source. finalize's re-derivation leaves any source other than
evidence_derived alone, so the value reaches the artifact.

